   "text": {
    "L1": "A table gives two counts. How many more asks for the gap between them.",
    "L2": "Do not subtract digits in the wrong order. Picture the two whole amounts first.",
    "L3": "For 785 and 563, 785 is bigger, so take the smaller count from the bigger count.",
    "L4": "Write the counts in columns and subtract: 785 minus 563 equals 222.",
    "L5": "If a column needs help, borrow from the next column. Do not simply take the smaller digit from the bigger digit.",
    "L6": "Check a difference by adding it back to the smaller count. 563 plus 222 equals 785.",
    "L7": "The same idea works for larger counts. In the worked example, 1308 minus 976 equals 332.",
    "L8": "Now choose the gap for 785 and 563."
   },
